# Vito, Fanatic of Aclazotz sacrificed together with an Ornithopter as Bankrupt in Blood's additional cost (CR 701.21a, 601.2h): it leaves the
# battlefield at the same time as the Ornithopter and so sees it sacrificed (CR 603.10a), and its trigger, for "another permanent", is
# one for the Ornithopter only: the first resolution of the turn, +2 life (22), never +4 for Vito itself. Nothing else changes: Bot2's
# life is still 20, no Demon is made, and Bankrupt in Blood draws its three cards.

